WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.359
The first trailer for Ant-Man and the Wasp
just dropped revealing a ton of cool new characters

00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:08.500
and details we can look forward to seeing
in the Ant-Man sequel.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.639
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm breaking down the new trailer

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:16.810
and explaining some easter eggs, wicked details
and other stuff you might have missed!

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:21.869
If you're new to my channel I do regular comic-book
movie videos, and to celebrate the first Ant-Man

00:00:21.869 --> 00:00:25.730
and the Wasp trailer, I'm kicking off a new
superhero giveaway for all my subscribers.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.830
I've got full details on that giveaway later
in this video.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:34.620
Ant-Man and the Wasp begins in the aftermath
of Captain America: Civil War.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.550
At the end of Civil War, Cap broke out Ant-Man
and the other Avengers who were locked up

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.079
in the Raft prison.

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:43.309
And in Ant-Man and the Wasp, it looks like
we'll find that the authorities have caught

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:46.370
up with Scott Lang, putting him under house
arrest.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:50.370
It's pretty clear though that once Hope van
Dyne and Hank Pym make contact with him again,

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.449
Scott isn't going to be at home very long.

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:54.800
Hope and Hank are on the run themselves.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.890
In fact, Hope blames that on Scott's Civil
War antics which might mean that their research

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:04.199
has come under scrutiny, and suggests why
Hank is using Pym particles to shrink down

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:06.031
his building into a portable piece of luggage.

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:11.960
The new mission that Hank and Hope contact
Scott about is their plan to bring back Hank's

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.590
wife, Janet van Dyne, from the Quantum Realm.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:18.820
In the first Ant-Man movie, Hank explained
that during their mission to deactivate a

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:23.400
bomb, Janet, who was the original Wasp, went
subatomic when she deactivated her regulator

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.030
to get inside the bomb.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.540
Though Scott went subatomic at the end of
that movie, he managed to return, which is

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:33.829
why Hank has been researching how they can
go to the Quantum Realm to bring back Janet,

00:01:33.829 --> 00:01:36.400
who in this movie will be played by Michelle
Pfieffer.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.229
And we might just have our first glimpse of
their journey into the Quantum Realm in this

00:01:41.229 --> 00:01:42.229
shot.

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:46.750
The creatures around them look at lot like
Tardigrades, aka water bears, which are real

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:52.540
eight-legged micro-animals and are about half
a millimetre or 0.02 inches long at their

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.950
full size.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:58.329
We don't know yet if this is the Quantum Realm
itself or just an interim stage where Hope

00:01:58.329 --> 00:02:02.710
and Scott shrink down their new craft until
they reach the subatomic level.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:07.200
The Quantum Realm has appeared briefly twice
before in the Marvel Cinematic Universe, first

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.160
at the end of Ant-Man and then again momentarily
in Doctor Strange when the Ancient One sent

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.890
Stephen Strange through the Multiverse when
he met her at Kamar-Taj.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.810
Obviously, we've got to talk about Hope van
Dyne's The Wasp.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:23.410
The trailer showcases an awesome power set
for the new hero.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:27.340
In addition to Ant-Man's shrinking powers,
she can fly and shoot power blasts.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:32.030
The blasters are a nice touch because, in
the comics, Hank Pym gave the Wasp wrist devices

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:35.710
which could produce electrified blasts that
she named "wasp stings".

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:41.150
And I just love how Wasp shows she's a literal
blade runner in this very cool slo-mo shot

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:45.760
of her running down the side of these knives,
which echoes Ant-Man's gun-running antics

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.970
in the first movie.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:52.210
And when the Wasp throws the Hello Kitty pez
dispenser, it's another cool callback to the

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:57.290
first movie when Ant-Man turned a Thomas the
Tank Engine toy giant-size.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:02.380
On top of that, the Hello Kitty nod also adds
a little Deadpool vibe, especially given that

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:07.610
the popular Marvel character could be joining
the MCU if Disney's deal with Fox goes ahead.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:12.730
Now, you'll need to look very carefully, but
we do get a super-brief look at the villainous

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:18.080
character Sonny Burch played by Walton Goggins,
and he appears to have stolen Pym's miniaturised

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.230
building!

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:23.560
In the comics, Sonny Burch is the chairman
of Cross Technologies and, in Ant-Man and

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:28.210
the Wasp, it seems he could be trying to steal
Pym's secrets to either get revenge for or

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:33.460
take advantage of the demise of Pym's former
protégé Darren Cross in the first movie.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:37.630
And that looks like the reason we get the
return of Giant-Man, who we see towering over

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:41.210
the boat, presumably to recover the stolen
property.

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:45.630
The trailer also gives us a quick tease of
the new villain Ghost who's played by Hannah

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:46.960
John-Kamen.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.590
In the comics, Ghost is actually male and
is an elite hacker who can make himself invisible

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:53.830
and phase through objects.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:57.750
And that might be what's going on here where
we can see an arm flickering and phasing in

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.220
and out of view.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:04.580
The comic-book version of Ghost uses his abilities
to attack and destroy corporations and I wonder

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:08.610
whether the MCU's Ghost could be connected
to the villainous Hydra?

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:12.990
You might recall that Hydra agents attended
Darren Cross's presentation in the Ant-Man

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:18.511
movie and one of the attendees, Mitchell Carson,
managed to escape with a vial of Pym particles

00:04:18.511 --> 00:04:20.400
before the building exploded.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.720
So, perhaps Ghost could be working for Hydra,
and it's also quite possible that she's working

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.410
together with Walton Goggins' character Sonny
Burch.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:34.310
The trailer also gives us a quick peek at
Laurence Fishburne who's playing Dr Bill Foster,

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.730
aka Goliath.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:40.190
In the comics, Dr Foster is a scientist who
worked for both Tony Stark and Hank Pym, and,

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:44.810
when he became familiar with how Pym Particles
worked, he experimented on himself, creating

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:47.580
his giant-sized alter ego, Goliath.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:51.860
He's traditionally a good guy, so it's quite
likely he'll team up with Scott, Hope and

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:52.860
Hank.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.730
However, while the trailer doesn't reveal
a lot about Dr Foster, the way it's edited

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:01.310
may imply he could be connected with Ghost
or the bad guys at some point.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:05.750
By the way, appropriately enough, the music
in the trailer is called "Ants Invasion" and

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:08.380
is by the British band Adam and the Ants!

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:12.710
